# labwc autostart entry for kitchen-display
#
# labwc runs this file only once the compositor is up, so every start line here is
# correctly ordered by construction -- the old `sleep 1` / `sleep 2` chain was
# cargo-culted and is gone. The kiosk, the static HTTP server and the idle policy
# are systemd user units, so systemd supervises and restarts them; autostart only
# asks for them.
#
# The idle timers live in kitchen-idle-policy.service, not here: the screen-off
# timeout depends on the time of day (5 h in 06:00-22:00, 30 min otherwise) and
# swayidle cannot reload its timeouts, so the policy re-arms swayidle at the
# window edge. Do not put an inline `swayidle` line back -- it would hold a stale
# timeout that wins over the policy (#32).
#
# graphical-session.target cannot be used as the trigger: it is
# RefuseManualStart=yes and does not activate on this image, so the units are
# started by name instead of through a session target.
systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP XDG_SESSION_TYPE
(systemctl --user start kitchen-display-http.service) &
(systemctl --user start kitchen-display.service) &
(systemctl --user start kitchen-idle-policy.service) &
(pgrep -x kanshi >/dev/null || kanshi) &
